# An interval with 2-limb bounds split at its midpoint (milestone2.md, "One enclosure interface", the
# row of split() and "The empty set and the whole line"): [xl, m] and [m, xu], m the midpoint of
# interval_mid_rad_2, which is in [xl, xu]; their union is the interval. The whole line gives [-inf,
# 0] and [0, +inf], a half-line [l, +inf] gives [l, Omega] and [Omega, +inf], and the empty set the
# empty set twice. One step more than for one limb: a bound of two limbs can be beyond Omega (Omega plus less than half a
# gap), and the midpoint +-Omega of a half-line is then outside the interval; the point of the split
# is the midpoint moved into [xl, xu] by lt_2_2, the bound itself in that case. The midpoint is
# computed by the steps of interval_mid_rad_2 that make it, without its radius: interval_mid_rad_2 is
# not called, since the radius would be unused (compilers remove its fused operations, which the
# object-code check counts), and the empty set is told by the lower bound, +inf.
kernel:        interval_split_2
input:         xl = xl0 xl1
input:         xu = xu0 xu1
output:        al = al0 al1
output:        au = au0 au1
output:        bl = bl0 bl1
output:        bu = bu0 bu1
requires:      interval xl xu
ensures:       splits al au bl bu from=xl,xu
min_precision: 3
source:        the bounds and the midpoint of interval_mid_rad_2, moved into the interval (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the midpoint is selected after the test of the lower bound that tells the empty set; splits states what comes out for every canonical interval

om         = pred(const inf)
mo         = neg(om)
ml         = lt(xl0, mo)
l0         = select(ml, mo, xl0)
l1         = select(ml, 0, xl1)
mu         = lt(om, xu0)
h0         = select(mu, om, xu0)
h1         = select(mu, 0, xu1)
(hl0, hl1) = mul_pow2_2(l0, l1, const up(1/2))
(hu0, hu1) = mul_pow2_2(h0, h1, const up(1/2))
(ma0, ma1) = add_2_2(hl0, hl1, hu0, hu1)
ca         = lt_2_2(ma0, ma1, l0, l1)
mb0        = select(ca, l0, ma0)
mb1        = select(ca, l1, ma1)
cb         = lt_2_2(h0, h1, mb0, mb1)
mc0        = select(cb, h0, mb0)
mc1        = select(cb, h1, mb1)
md0        = select(ml, mo, mc0)
md1        = select(ml, 0, mc1)
me0        = select(mu, om, md0)
me1        = select(mu, 0, md1)
bo         = and(ml, mu)
m0         = select(bo, 0, me0)
m1         = select(bo, 0, me1)
ka         = lt_2_2(m0, m1, xl0, xl1)
n0         = select(ka, xl0, m0)
n1         = select(ka, xl1, m1)
kb         = lt_2_2(xu0, xu1, n0, n1)
p0         = select(kb, xu0, n0)
p1         = select(kb, xu1, n1)
ne         = lt(xl0, const inf)
mi         = neg(const inf)
al0        = copy(xl0)
al1        = copy(xl1)
au0        = select(ne, p0, mi)
au1        = select(ne, p1, 0)
bl0        = select(ne, p0, const inf)
bl1        = select(ne, p1, 0)
bu0        = copy(xu0)
bu1        = copy(xu1)
